cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite both the dataset and the paper it belongs to."
title: "Data release for: First Search for Ultraheavy Dark Matter Using a Magnetically Levitated Particle"
abstract: >-
  The complete limit-setting calculation behind the first ultraheavy dark matter
  search with a magnetically levitated particle, as one self-describing HDF5
  file. Over a grid in dark-matter fraction, atmospheric propagation, sensor
  mode, per-neutron coupling, dark-matter mass and mediator range it stores the
  optimum-interval extremeness, the expected detected signal, and the expected
  number of in-reach transits, together with the measured per-mode detection
  efficiency curves, the impulse candidate lists and the live time. Exclusion at
  any confidence level is a level set of the stored extremeness.
type: dataset
version: "v5.0-night-m0p356mg-bcap10cm"
date-released: "2026-08-08"
